# expect: unterminated_hole.or:8:8 - unterminated `{` in a string
# This HUNG THE COMPILER FOREVER. `"{{"` opens an interpolation hole whose
# content lexes to a bare `{`; that reached the map-literal parser, which had no
# no-progress guard and spun. A hang is worse than any error message, and
# nothing in the suite could have caught it: negative_test.sh now runs each case
# under a timeout so a spin is a failure, not a stuck run.
define main() -> number:
    s = "{{"
    length(s)
